rd of Directors of Paychex, Inc. (Nasdaq: PAYX) declared a regular quarterly cash dividend on Paychex common stock of $1.08 per share, payable on August 29, 2025, to shareholders of record as of July 21, 2025.\n\nBy Paychex, Inc. · Via Business Wire · July 9, 2025\n\nU.S. Small Business Employment Holds Steady Through First Half of 2025\n\nThe small business labor market has remained stable with minimal changes observed through the first half of 2025, according to the Paychex Small Business Employment Watch. The pace of job growth in U.S. businesses with fewer than 50 employees has fluctuated less than half a percentage point over the last six months, reporting a 99.65 index level for June. At the same time, hourly earnings growth for small business workers continued to trend below three percent at 2.79%.\n\nBy Paychex, Inc. · Via Business Wire · July 1, 2025\n\nPaychex, Inc. Reports Fourth Quarter and Full Year 2025 Results\n\nPaychex, Inc. (Nasdaq: PAYX) (the \"Company,\" \"Paychex,\" \"we,\" \"our,\" or \"us\") today reported results for the fiscal quarter ended May 31, 2025 (the \"fourth quarter\") and fiscal year ended May 31, 2025 (\"fiscal 2025\"). Results compared with the same period last year are as follows:\n\nBy Paychex, Inc. · Via Business Wire · June 25, 2025\n\nPaychex, Inc. Schedules Fourth Quarter Fiscal 2025 Earnings Conference Call for June 25, 2025\n\nPaychex, Inc. (Nasdaq: PAYX) will release financial results for its fiscal 2025 fourth quarter ended May 31, 2025 before the financial markets open on Wednesday, June 25, 2025.\n\nBy Paychex, Inc. · Via Business Wire · June 13, 2025\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDEF 14A (https://investor.paychex.com/sec-filings/all-sec-filings/content/0001193125-25-191789/d946290ddef14a.htm)\nciteturn12search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.2 years ago; Crawled: today; \nStockholder Distributions: The value we return to our stockholders is very important to us. During fiscal 2025, we distributed $1.6 billion to our stockholders through dividends and repurchases of outstanding shares of our common stock.\n\n \n\n |  |  |  | \n |     |   We have distributed  $6.4 billion to stockholders over the  past 5 years.     |     | \n\n \n\n |  |  |  | \nImage: LOGO  |     |  |     | Image: LOGO\n\n \n\nDividend Payments: We continue to pay substantial dividends to our stockholders. The most recent increases in the quarterly dividend to stockholders were as follows:\n\n \n\n |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | \n |  |  | \n    |     | Increase in Quarterly\nDividend  |     | Quarterly Dividend Amount  |     | % Change \n |  |  | \nMay 2025  |     |    | $  | 0.10  |  |     |    | $  | 1.08  |  |     |    |    | 10  | %\n |  |  | \nMay 2024  |     |    | $  | 0.09  |  |     |    | $  | 0.98  |  |     |    |    | 10  | %\n |  |  | \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www.whnstv.marketminute.com/article/publisher/Paychex%2C%20Inc.)\nciteturn12search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; \n\nBy Paychex, Inc. · Via Business Wire · July 23, 2025\n\nPaychex and SoFi at Work Join Forces to Expand Financial Well-being Offerings\n\nPaychex, Inc., an industry-leading human capital management (HCM) company, announced today a new partnership with SoFi, a one stop shop for digital finance solutions, to bring the financial well-being resources and solutions of SoFi at Work to users of Paychex Flex® Perks. Through Paychex’s digital marketplace of curated employee benefits, employees of Paychex customers can seamlessly connect to SoFi’s solutions to support their journey to financial independence, including personal loans, student loans, loan refinancing, and more.\n\nBy Paychex, Inc. · Via Business Wire · July 17, 2025\n\nPaychex Declares Quarterly Dividend\n\nThe Board of Directors of Paychex, Inc. (Nasdaq: PAYX) declared a regular quarterly cash dividend on Paychex common stock of $1.08 per share, payable on August 29, 2025, to shareholders of record as of July 21, 2025.\n\nBy Paychex, Inc. · Via Business Wire · July 9, 2025\n\nU.S. Small Business Employment Holds Steady Through First Half of 2025\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn12view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20250424490742/en/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: Failed to fetch https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20250424490742/en/: Cache miss\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn12view1 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20250709281818/en/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: Failed to fetch https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20250709281818/en/: Cache miss\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGLOBE LIFE INC. DECLARES DIVIDEND (https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/globe-life-inc-declares-dividend-302437556.html)\nciteturn12view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn11view0\",\"pattern\":\"quarterly dividend\"}); Total lines: 586\nL467: ## News provided by\nL468: \nL469: 【303†Globe Life Inc.】\nL470: \nL471: Apr 24, 2025, 16:15 ET\nL472: \nL473: * * *\nL474: \nL475: MCKINNEY, Texas, April 24, 2025 /PRNewswire/ -- Globe Life Inc. (NYSE: 【304†GL】) announced that its Board of Directors has declared a quarterly dividend of $.2700 per share on all of the outstanding common stock of the Company held of record as of close of business of the Company's transfer agent on July 3, 2025. The dividend will be paid on August 1, 2025.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA. O. Smith Reports Quarterly Dividend | A. O. Smith Corporation (https://aosmith.gcs-web.com/news-releases/news-releas